Inclusion Criteria:

1. Unexplained cramps occurred two or more times in 2 weeks.
2. Age ≥65-year-old.

Exclusion criteria

1. Cramps caused by specific metabolic diseases and specific neuropathies (hypothyroidism, hemodialysis, hypoglycemia, alcoholism, amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, and poliomyelitis complications, lumbar spinal stenosis, Parkinson's disease, radiculopathies, and motor neuron diseases);
2. Suffering from malignant tumors (breast cancer, prostate cancer, lymphoma, and multiple myeloma);
