15. Long-term use (continuous use ≥14 days) of immunosuppressants or other immunomodulatory drugs (such as corticosteroids: prednisone or similar drugs) within the 6 months prior to the study vaccine, but topical use (such as ointment, eye drops, inhalants or nasal spray) is permitted, and the topical use shall not exceed the dosage recommended in the instructions or any systemic signs of exposure;
